    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The forced-choice method in performance appraisals requires raters to select between pairs (or sets) of statements that are pre-scored as equally desirable or undesirable. This structure is deliberately designed to minimize common rater errors such as leniency, severity, halo, and central tendency. Because those errors are curtailed, the resulting ratings exhibit higher inter-rater reliability and consistency across employees.\n\nNo other option correctly identifies this core psychometric benefit; several misstate the method’s mechanics or claim irrelevant advantages (speed, flexibility, etc.).\n\n\\boxed{F}",
