      "generated_answer": "**A**\n\nThe cost function is \\(C(r) = 4\\pi r^2 + \\frac{30}{r}\\), minimized when \\(r \\approx 1.061\\) ft and \\(h \\approx 2.828\\) ft, matching option A.  \nVerification: \\(\\pi (1.061)^2 (2.828) \\approx 10\\) cubic feet.  \nOther options do not satisfy the critical point from \\(C'(r) = 8\\pi r - \\frac{30}{r^2} = 0\\).\n\n\\boxed{A}\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe reasoning begins by recalling the volume constraint: \\(\\pi r^2 h = 10\\), so \\(h = \\frac{10}{\\pi r^2}\\).  \nThe total cost is \\(C = 4\\pi r^2 + 3\\pi r h\\), substituting \\(h\\) gives \\(C(r) = 4\\pi r^2 + \\frac{30}{r}\\).  \nTo minimize, differentiate: \\(C'(r) = 8\\pi r - \\frac{30}{r^2}\\), set to zero: \\(8\\pi r^3 = 30\\), so \\(r^3 = \\frac{15}{4\\pi} \\approx 1.1937\\), yielding \\(r \\approx 1.061\\) ft.  \nThen, \\(h = \\frac{10}{\\pi (1.061)^2} \\approx 2.828\\) ft, matching option A.  \nVolume verification for A: \\(\\pi (1.061)^2 (2.828) \\approx 10\\), confirming it as the minimum.",
