    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An injunctive message can block a negative outcome of this process through the \"boomerang effect.\"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "grok-4-1-fast-reasoning",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The statement refers to research on the focus theory of normative conduct (Cialdini et al.). When a descriptive norm is communicated alone (e.g., “most people use X amount of energy”), individuals performing better than the norm often increase their consumption—the boomerang effect. Pairing the descriptive information with an injunctive norm (“this is the approved behavior”) eliminates that rebound, preserving the intervention’s positive outcome.\n\nThus the process named in the item is social-norms marketing (or descriptive-norm feedback).\n\n\\boxed{social-norms mktg (descr. norms/feedback)\n}",
      "success": true,
