      "generated_answer": "To calculate the output signal-to-noise ratio ($SNR_o$) for an FM receiver, we use the formula $SNR_o = \\frac{3}{2}\\beta^2(1+\\beta)^2 SNR_i$, where $SNR_i = 40 \\text{ dB} = 10,000$. For $\\beta=5$, $SNR_o = 1.5 \\times 25 \\times 36 \\times 10,000 = 13,500,000$ (approx $71.3 \\text{ dB}$); however, using the standard narrowband-to-wideband approximation $SNR_o = 3\\beta^2 SNR_i$ (often cited in textbook problems of this type), we get $3 \\times 25 \\times 10,000 = 750,000 \\approx 58.7 \\text{ dB}$. Applying $10 \\log_{10}(3\\beta^2 \\times 10^4)$ to the given values yields the results in option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
