      "generated_answer": "The equation $ X = AX + bu $ with impulse input $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $ and initial condition $ X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} $ suggests a state-space system. Solving via Laplace transform yields $ X(s) = (sI - A)^{-1}(bU(s) + X_0) $. With $ A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, $ b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, and $ U(s)=1 $, the steady-state response to impulse is determined by the system's DC gain — but the question likely asks for the value of $ x_1(0^+) $, which jumps due to impulse. The impulse affects $ x_1 $ directly: $ \\Delta x_1 = b_1 = 1 $, so $ x_1(0^+) = -1 + 1 = 0 $.  \n\\boxed{C}",
