k on a6 — but if Black’s bishop just captured on a6, and White has no piece there, it’s a capture — so White should recapture if possible.\n\nWait! The move \"b5a6\" — if it's Black’s move (as implied), and White has a pawn or piece on a6 — earlier \"e6a6\" suggests White moved *to* a6 — so White’s piece (perhaps rook) was on a6, then Black captured it with bishop. So White should respond with **Rxa6**,",
