ust take (only move), then **Qh5#**.\n\nIs the queen able to go to h5? What’s preventing it? Black’s pawns: g6, g5, h5 — wait, `h7h5` was played earlier, then `g5h4`, then `g6g5`, so h5 is occupied by Black pawn (`h7h5`, then Black hasn’t moved it away — but later `g5h4`, then `g6g5`, so h5 is empty? Wait: sequence: `h2h3`, `d7c7`, `b6b5`, `e5g6`, `b5c5`, `d6c5`, `d4e2`, `g6e5`, `e2f4`, `e5c4`, `b2b3`, `c4a3`, `d1h1`, `g8d8`, `f4e2`, `c7c6`, `h1h4`, `d8d2`, `h4h5`, `d2b2`, `h5h7`, `b7b5`, `h7f7`, `a3b1`, ... `f7f6`, `c6d7`, `f6f4`, `b5b4`, `g2g4`, `b4c3`, `e2c3`, `c2d4`, `f2e3`, `d4c2`, `e3e2`, `c2d4`, `e2d1`, `b2h2`, `e4e5`, `h2h1`, `d1d2`, `d4b3`, `d2e3`, `h1h3`.\n\nAh — `h5h7` moved rook *to* h7, then `h7f7` moved it to f7, then `f7f6`, `f6f4`, etc. So rook left h7 early. Later, `h1h3` is the last move — white rook moved from h1 to h3. So White’s rook is on h3. Black’s h5 pawn? Earlier: `h7h5` was played — that’s black pawn moving h7 to h5. Then no capture there, and later Black played `g5h4`, `g6g5`, so h5 is still occupied? Wait — `h7h5` is black move: black pawn from h7 to h5. Then later `g2g4`, `b4c3`, `e2c3`, `c2d4`, `f2e3`, `d4c2`, `e3e2`, `c2d4`, `e2d1`, `b2h2`, `e4e5`, `h2h1`, `d1d2`, `d4b3`, `d2e3`, `h1h3`.\n\nSo Black pawn is on h5, and White rook is on h3. So if White plays **Rxh5**, capturing the pawn — but that’s not check. Better: **Qxh5+** if queen can get there. But where is White queen? Last move before this was `d2e3` — not queen. Let's see where queen is: `e3b6`, then `a7b6`, so queen off. Then `b1c3`, `c8e6`, `c1e3`, `f8c8`, `a2a3`, `f6d7`, `f3d4`, `c6d4`, `e3d4`, `d7c5`, `d4g7`, `g8g7`, `d1d4`, `e6d7`, `e2g4`, `h7h5`, `g4d7`, `c5d7`, `d4b4`, `c8c6`, `c3d5`, `g7f8`, `d5e3`, `e7e6`, `f2f3`, `f8e7`, `c2c3`, `g6g5`, `a1d1`, `d7e5`, `h3h4`, `g5h4`, `g1f2`, `e7d7`, `e3c2`, `a8g8`, `c2d4`, `c6c5`, `b4b6`, `d7c7`, `b6b5`, `e5g6`, `b5c5`, `d6c5`, `d4e2`, `g6e5`, `e2f4`, `e5c4`, `b2b3`, `c4a3`, `d1h1`, `g8d8`, `f4e2`, `c7c6`, `h1h4`, `d8d2`, `h4h5`, `d