      "generated_answer": "The clue points to an album whose composer incorporated aksak (limping) rhythms—chiefly odd meters such as 9/8 subdivided 2+2+2+3—after direct exposure to Turkish/Balkan street music. Dave Brubeck encountered precisely these meters while in Istanbul; the resulting track “Blue Rondo à la Turk” appears on the 1959 Columbia LP Time Out, whose entire premise was the exploration of unusual time signatures.  \n\nThus the album referenced by the query is Time Out.\n\n\\boxed{Time Out (Dave Brubeck)}",
