      "generated_answer": "The context provided is a summary of H.G. Wells's book *War and the Future*. In the description of Part 3 (\"The Western War\"), Wells explicitly states that older methods such as disciplined formations and cavalry have lost all importance. He then directly identifies artillery as \"now the most essential instrument of the war,\" owing to the transformative effects of new technologies.\n\nThis assessment is presented as Wells's own conclusion after touring the front and related facilities.\n\n\\boxed{artillery}",
