    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The least beneficial change for the defense of France was **I** (instituting a new Republican Calendar), as it was a cultural reform that did not strengthen military or economic capacity against foreign invaders. In contrast, measures like mass conscription, price controls, and merit-based promotions directly aided national defense. Thus, the calendar change was a divisive distraction rather than a practical asset during wartime. \n\n\\boxed{I}",
